      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T15:38:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e VisibleForTesting does not mean the function exists for testing\n\nYeah, basically @VFT(NONE) means that function literally exists for testing.\n\nWhile we are at this topic, I should also mention sort of a similar annotation @RestrictTo which has an enum called TESTS (https://developer.android.com/reference/android/support/annotation/RestrictTo.Scope.html#tests). While it does looks more readable, but it has limited set of enums that it can support, so my preference in general between these to has been @VFT",
      "parentUuid": "b2c5706c_e0452ffe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 848,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 848,
        "endChar": 36
      },
